@IdentityService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5001

### Register — always Client, 201 without token
POST {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "fullName": "John Doe"
}

###

### Register duplicate → 409
POST {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123",
  "fullName": "John Doe"
}

###

### Register validation 400 (short password)
POST {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bad@example.com",
  "password": "short",
  "fullName": "Bad"
}

###

### Login — 200 with token
# @name login
POST {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123"
}

###

### Login invalid → 401
POST {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpass"
}

###

### Me — 200 with Bearer token
GET {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

###

### Me without token → 401
GET {{IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me

###
